1
00:00:05,794 --> 00:00:06,624
Jinguji!

2
00:00:11,614 --> 00:00:13,908
Are you trying to get crushed to death?

3
00:00:14,254 --> 00:00:15,834
I'm sorry, Tachibana.

4
00:00:16,134 --> 00:00:19,016
I had no idea I'd been
causing you all this pain.

5
00:00:19,694 --> 00:00:20,654
Whoa, you okay?

6
00:00:22,494 --> 00:00:26,654
The thing is, in my entire life
I've never once praised anyone.

7
00:00:26,894 --> 00:00:28,111
Even now I can't do it.

8
00:00:28,194 --> 00:00:29,271
I don't know how.

9
00:00:29,354 --> 00:00:31,914
Then you might suck as a person?

10
00:00:34,254 --> 00:00:35,931
Chartsie, stay out of this!

11
00:00:36,014 --> 00:00:37,074
What?

12
00:00:37,454 --> 00:00:41,451
Now that's cheating All of my
direct attacks just get deflected.

13
00:00:41,534 --> 00:00:43,671
I'll knock off the arms if I punch again!

14
00:00:43,754 --> 00:00:44,674
Right?

15
00:00:53,934 --> 00:00:55,634
How do you like this?

16
00:01:01,274 --> 00:01:05,039
Those thoughts, I think maybe
it's true that I suck as a person.

17
00:01:05,214 --> 00:01:08,791
Go ahead, you're still stuck on
that when we're about to die?

18
00:01:08,874 --> 00:01:12,992
How can I help when I end up hurting
people just by being around them?

19
00:01:13,714 --> 00:01:16,071
I never considered that
what I thought was helpful

20
00:01:16,154 --> 00:01:19,330
criticism could come off as
judgmental or patronizing,

21
00:01:19,414 --> 00:01:22,811
but if someone mistook my intent,
of course they would be hurt by it.

22
00:01:22,894 --> 00:01:23,724
Jigun!

23
00:01:23,807 --> 00:01:24,637
Jigunji, help me!

24
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:28,591
And for it to come from someone you
consider to be your best friend,

25
00:01:28,674 --> 00:01:31,733
someone you believe is
better than you in every way?

26
00:01:32,034 --> 00:01:34,654
it's no wonder Tachibana
is in so much pain.

27
00:01:36,234 --> 00:01:39,528
I think it would be best if
I disappeared from his life.

28
00:01:39,614 --> 00:01:41,931
Weren't you listening to
a single word he said?

29
00:01:42,014 --> 00:01:42,844
Huh?

30
00:01:42,927 --> 00:01:44,062
He literally just told you.

31
00:01:44,154 --> 00:01:47,391
The only thing he takes pride in is
the fact that you're his best friend.

32
00:01:47,474 --> 00:01:50,391
So even though he's completely
unhinged and trying to kill us,

33
00:01:50,474 --> 00:01:52,239
you're still important to him.

34
00:01:52,914 --> 00:01:55,451
It's hard for people to admit
what they really care about,

35
00:01:55,534 --> 00:01:57,411
especially when they're in a bad place.

36
00:01:57,494 --> 00:01:59,631
Him opening up like this is a huge deal!

37
00:01:59,714 --> 00:02:03,471
And if you were to walk out on him
now after everything that's happened,

38
00:02:03,554 --> 00:02:07,554
you wouldn't be protecting him,
you'd be hurting him all over again!

39
00:02:07,674 --> 00:02:09,411
Ethan, what am I supposed to do?

40
00:02:09,494 --> 00:02:11,811
He's been telling you what
to do this whole time!

41
00:02:11,894 --> 00:02:15,070
He wants you to compliment
him, so just do it already!

42
00:02:15,534 --> 00:02:17,991
I thought I did, but it
just made him angrier.

43
00:02:18,074 --> 00:02:20,511
That's because what you told
him didn't mean anything to you!

44
00:02:20,594 --> 00:02:22,551
He needs to know how you
feel from the bottom of your

45
00:02:22,634 --> 00:02:25,611
heart something that shows
him how important he is to you

46
00:02:25,694 --> 00:02:27,459
Do you think I don't get that?

47
00:02:28,114 --> 00:02:28,991
But still...

48
00:02:29,074 --> 00:02:30,154
Come on!

49
00:02:30,374 --> 00:02:32,492
This shouldn't be that hard for you!

50
00:02:33,074 --> 00:02:33,904
Well...

51
00:02:34,214 --> 00:02:37,332
Isn't it embarrassing to
confess something like that?

52
00:02:37,894 --> 00:02:40,014
ARE YOU KIDDING ME?!

53
00:02:40,974 --> 00:02:42,571
Hey, what was that for?!

54
00:02:42,654 --> 00:02:43,694
SHUT UP!

55
00:02:44,154 --> 00:02:47,131
Your bizarre lover's quarrel
is endangering a whole kingdom!

56
00:02:47,214 --> 00:02:48,851
Imagine how it feels for all of us!

57
00:02:48,934 --> 00:02:50,014
Lover's claw?

58
00:02:50,674 --> 00:02:54,351
You're a thirty-something-year-old man,
but you've been acting like a whiny teen!

59
00:02:54,434 --> 00:02:58,371
You even got jealous because the princess
started hanging out with Tachibana!

60
00:02:58,454 --> 00:03:02,114
I already told you, I
wasn't jealous! That's it!

61
00:03:02,294 --> 00:03:03,951
That's the problem right there!

62
00:03:04,034 --> 00:03:06,631
You can't admit you're
jealous or care about him

63
00:03:06,714 --> 00:03:09,655
when it's a totally normal
guy-friend thing to do!

64
00:03:10,874 --> 00:03:11,774
It's normal?

65
00:03:15,534 --> 00:03:18,694
So that means you felt that way?

66
00:03:19,374 --> 00:03:20,204
With a man?

67
00:03:20,834 --> 00:03:21,664
Seriously?

68
00:03:21,874 --> 00:03:25,191
When my friend Yamazato stopped hanging
out with me after he got a girlfriend,

69
00:03:25,274 --> 00:03:28,980
I got stupid jealous, but I dealt
with it like a normal person!

70
00:03:29,174 --> 00:03:31,091
Keeping Tachipane at arm's
length because he's a

71
00:03:31,174 --> 00:03:33,451
dude is weirder than
admitting he's special to you!

72
00:03:33,534 --> 00:03:37,631
And you being self-conscious about the
whole thing only adds to the weirdness.

73
00:03:37,714 --> 00:03:39,094
I see. Thank you.

74
00:03:39,814 --> 00:03:41,734
I think I finally understand.

75
00:03:44,574 --> 00:03:47,654
As a child, I was taught
to never rely on others.

76
00:03:48,494 --> 00:03:51,200
Those who did were seen
as selfish or spoiled.

77
00:03:52,374 --> 00:03:53,454
Never falter.

78
00:03:53,934 --> 00:03:55,291
Carry yourself with dignity.

79
00:03:55,374 --> 00:03:56,903
Be the example to society.

80
00:03:57,854 --> 00:04:00,194
These ideas were drilled into me.

81
00:04:03,894 --> 00:04:05,334
Never appear as weak.

82
00:04:05,834 --> 00:04:07,305
Never show vulnerability.

83
00:04:08,434 --> 00:04:12,728
That was how I could become strong
enough to survive the world on my own.

84
00:04:13,214 --> 00:04:18,174
I came to believe that if I were to bare
my soul, I'd be risking myself for nothing.

85
00:04:20,194 --> 00:04:21,024
But...

86
00:04:21,834 --> 00:04:23,811
Guys can be jealous over each other!

87
00:04:23,894 --> 00:04:25,718
It's a completely normal thing!

88
00:04:27,894 --> 00:04:30,674
You agree? What? Oh, yeah! Of course!

89
00:04:30,914 --> 00:04:32,385
You can do what you want!

90
00:04:33,894 --> 00:04:35,074
I think I will!

91
00:04:37,854 --> 00:04:38,684
Got him!

92
00:04:42,694 --> 00:04:44,929
It's high time I let myself be honest.

93
00:04:45,174 --> 00:04:47,174
I owe that much to my best friend.

94
00:04:47,394 --> 00:04:49,814
That and more, right, Schwartz? Ha!

95
00:04:50,054 --> 00:04:51,289
One thousand percent!

96
00:04:51,614 --> 00:04:53,254
Why are you doing this?

97
00:04:53,394 --> 00:04:55,751
I've kept this paint
bottled up for so long!

98
00:04:55,834 --> 00:04:58,651
The least you can do is
let me take it out on you!

99
00:04:58,734 --> 00:05:01,111
Why try this hard to stop me?!

100
00:05:01,194 --> 00:05:05,011
And all I really want to do is
feel a little better about myself!

101
00:05:05,094 --> 00:05:07,214
I've always envied you, Tachibana.

102
00:05:08,254 --> 00:05:11,911
You make friends everywhere you go,
and no matter where you might be,

103
00:05:11,994 --> 00:05:14,053
you're always surrounded by smiles.

104
00:05:15,314 --> 00:05:19,074
Just being part of your life
is enough to warm my heart.

105
00:05:19,834 --> 00:05:22,791
Earlier you said you were sick of
being a person who has nothing.

106
00:05:22,874 --> 00:05:26,131
How could you think that when your life
is filled with so much more than mine?

107
00:05:26,214 --> 00:05:28,554
I wish you could see what I see in you.

108
00:05:30,014 --> 00:05:32,308
And yet, after all your years together,

109
00:05:32,494 --> 00:05:35,391
you still don't have a clue
about how he truly feels.

110
00:05:35,474 --> 00:05:37,650
Why would you trust anything he says?

111
00:05:37,734 --> 00:05:39,969
He's never been truly honest with you.

112
00:05:40,474 --> 00:05:42,474
You know how clever he is.

113
00:05:42,874 --> 00:05:46,311
Imagine how easy it would be for
him to hide his true feelings.

114
00:05:46,394 --> 00:05:50,570
Just like how you were able to hide
your jealousy of him all this time.

115
00:05:51,074 --> 00:05:51,904
That's right.

116
00:05:51,987 --> 00:05:54,851
I bet deep down you're just laughing
at how much of a loser I am.

117
00:05:54,934 --> 00:05:57,191
The loser who's jealous
of his best friend,

118
00:05:57,274 --> 00:05:59,051
who complains about how
unfair the world is?

119
00:05:59,134 --> 00:06:00,891
because he doesn't have
any special talents.

120
00:06:00,974 --> 00:06:02,311
It didn't matter what I did.

121
00:06:02,394 --> 00:06:03,570
I never lasted long.

122
00:06:03,834 --> 00:06:07,191
The most I ever do is moan about
all the things I failed at.

123
00:06:07,274 --> 00:06:10,091
Meanwhile, you're out there
being perfect at everything.

124
00:06:10,174 --> 00:06:12,231
The difference between us was clear.

125
00:06:12,314 --> 00:06:14,531
You've earned tons of
awards and certificates.

126
00:06:14,614 --> 00:06:17,031
You're a student council
president and the student rep.

127
00:06:17,114 --> 00:06:18,643
And you're stupid popular.

128
00:06:22,234 --> 00:06:24,514
You never tolerated bullies or thugs.

129
00:06:24,934 --> 00:06:27,431
You saved those who
couldn't save themselves.

130
00:06:27,514 --> 00:06:31,161
I realized all of this the moment
we met back in grade school.

131
00:06:31,354 --> 00:06:34,531
You never talked at all, but
you still stood up for me.

132
00:06:34,614 --> 00:06:36,320
I didn't even know your name.

133
00:06:37,434 --> 00:06:38,994
Hey there, are you okay?

134
00:06:40,714 --> 00:06:43,234
Oh yeah, I was jealous.

135
00:06:43,754 --> 00:06:46,874
All this time, I wanted
to be just like you.

136
00:06:47,774 --> 00:06:49,074
Because to me.

137
00:06:51,154 --> 00:06:52,074
So cool.

138
00:06:54,934 --> 00:06:56,774
Leo, you look just like a hero!

139
00:07:02,874 --> 00:07:04,234
You are a hero!

140
00:07:04,674 --> 00:07:06,074
And I look up to you!

141
00:07:08,174 --> 00:07:09,586
Do you think it's weird?

142
00:07:10,434 --> 00:07:11,264
Sorta.

143
00:07:11,347 --> 00:07:14,509
I mean, wanting to be that
when you grow up is kinda...

144
00:07:16,254 --> 00:07:19,454
But hey, if it's what you
wanna do, that's cool.

145
00:07:20,034 --> 00:07:20,864
A hero.

146
00:07:31,834 --> 00:07:34,305
Oh, it sounds like Mepon is shutting down.

147
00:07:36,854 --> 00:07:38,754
Oh, does that touch Ivana?

148
00:07:39,074 --> 00:07:40,114
Yeah, that's him.

149
00:07:44,214 --> 00:07:45,314
Hang on a second.

150
00:07:45,514 --> 00:07:46,671
What is it doing now?

151
00:07:46,754 --> 00:07:47,584
Is this bad?

152
00:07:47,814 --> 00:07:49,520
Sounds like an error warning.

153
00:07:49,954 --> 00:07:51,294
Error! Error!

154
00:07:51,474 --> 00:07:54,356
Unknown interference with
energy source detected!

155
00:07:57,074 --> 00:07:57,904
Initiate.

156
00:07:57,987 --> 00:07:58,817
Transformation.

157
00:07:58,900 --> 00:08:00,194
To Resos Mode.

158
00:08:00,614 --> 00:08:04,673
Commencing extermination of all life
forms in the immediate vicinity.

159
00:08:05,174 --> 00:08:06,334
What's going on?

160
00:08:06,634 --> 00:08:07,494
Nothing good.

161
00:08:14,674 --> 00:08:16,234
Things just got worse!

162
00:08:16,614 --> 00:08:19,951
I think these are homing targets,
they'll stay on us no matter what!

163
00:08:20,034 --> 00:08:20,864
Seems like it.

164
00:08:20,947 --> 00:08:22,385
What are we gonna do now?

165
00:08:22,514 --> 00:08:26,191
Riso's smoke sounds scary enough, but now
we got literal targets on our foreheads.

166
00:08:26,274 --> 00:08:28,134
It's game over, man! Calm down.

167
00:08:29,134 --> 00:08:30,771
This doesn't change anything.

168
00:08:30,854 --> 00:08:32,560
Our goals are still the same.

169
00:08:32,874 --> 00:08:35,168
First, we're going to rescue Tachibana.

170
00:08:35,354 --> 00:08:38,530
After which, I'll destroy
Mepon before anyone is hurt.

171
00:08:38,674 --> 00:08:40,086
But I can't do it alone.

172
00:08:40,974 --> 00:08:41,804
So...

173
00:08:41,887 --> 00:08:42,717
Are you ready?

174
00:08:43,554 --> 00:08:44,384
Schwarz!

175
00:08:44,494 --> 00:08:45,612
I've got your back!

176
00:08:49,934 --> 00:08:51,874
Nice try! Take this!

177
00:08:56,854 --> 00:08:58,774
Now, Chinko-Chi! Right!

178
00:09:11,594 --> 00:09:14,971
Of all the things that crappy goddess
has done, she outdid herself with this!

179
00:09:15,054 --> 00:09:16,294
Give me back!

180
00:09:17,534 --> 00:09:19,474
My best friend!

181
00:09:30,674 --> 00:09:32,374
You alright, Tachibana?

182
00:09:32,774 --> 00:09:35,127
You look like you just got off a bender.

183
00:09:36,414 --> 00:09:38,674
Hey, are you okay?

184
00:09:43,614 --> 00:09:44,444
Jiguchi?

185
00:09:49,674 --> 00:09:50,504
Darn it!

186
00:09:50,587 --> 00:09:51,750
I let my guard down!

187
00:09:51,894 --> 00:09:54,659
I forgot how dangerous
those teary eyes can be!

188
00:09:57,434 --> 00:10:01,905
I'm sorry, you must think I'm pathetic
acting like a bratty child at my age.

189
00:10:02,214 --> 00:10:03,654
I really screwed up.

190
00:10:03,914 --> 00:10:08,149
You could have gotten killed, and I
nearly destroyed the entire kingdom!

191
00:10:08,534 --> 00:10:11,131
I let myself get caught
up in a dumb rebellion

192
00:10:11,214 --> 00:10:14,114
and ended up going on a robot rampage.

193
00:10:14,234 --> 00:10:15,834
I'm a garbage person.

194
00:10:16,394 --> 00:10:18,335
You have every reason to hate me.

195
00:10:18,954 --> 00:10:22,425
And I understand if you don't
want me in your life anymore.

196
00:10:27,634 --> 00:10:30,163
Tachibana, I'm only
going to say this once.

197
00:10:30,434 --> 00:10:31,594
So please listen.

198
00:10:33,554 --> 00:10:35,791
I think that you're amazing
and you're a good person.

199
00:10:35,874 --> 00:10:37,286
You're very considerate.

200
00:10:37,414 --> 00:10:39,191
You never forget to follow up with people.

201
00:10:39,274 --> 00:10:41,431
You always pay attention
and learn their needs.

202
00:10:41,514 --> 00:10:44,411
No matter what people might ask of
you, you give it to them in the end.

203
00:10:44,494 --> 00:10:47,511
You make friends easily, which to
me is a sign of good character.

204
00:10:47,594 --> 00:10:50,594
And it's something that
I've never been able to do.

205
00:10:51,794 --> 00:10:55,171
You're kind, and though bosses tend to
hate you, your juniors all love you.

206
00:10:55,254 --> 00:10:56,671
You have an upbeat attitude.

207
00:10:56,754 --> 00:10:59,891
Your smile brightens my day,
and you're an expressive person.

208
00:10:59,974 --> 00:11:01,331
Animals love to be around you.

209
00:11:01,414 --> 00:11:02,931
You never get full of yourself.

210
00:11:03,014 --> 00:11:05,451
You replace the toilet paper in
the bathroom when the rolls out.

211
00:11:05,534 --> 00:11:08,751
You're smarter than you give yourself
credit for, and you are athletic!

212
00:11:08,834 --> 00:11:11,431
You just think you're not because
you compare yourself to me.

213
00:11:11,514 --> 00:11:14,251
I've had dark times I couldn't
have gotten through without you.

214
00:11:14,334 --> 00:11:18,331
I admire your empathy and your bizarre
ability to get people to laugh at anything,

215
00:11:18,414 --> 00:11:19,791
like your terrible jokes.

216
00:11:19,874 --> 00:11:23,991
When you're around, the world is brighter,
and that saved me from many a bad day.

217
00:11:24,074 --> 00:11:25,611
You have the best ugly cry,

218
00:11:25,694 --> 00:11:28,671
especially when you watch videos of
cute animals or kids doing errands.

219
00:11:28,754 --> 00:11:32,131
And when something is clearly staged,
you can love it unapologetically.

220
00:11:32,214 --> 00:11:34,391
I like how you'll try
popular things just because.

221
00:11:34,474 --> 00:11:36,331
And after you found out I liked whiskey,

222
00:11:36,414 --> 00:11:38,931
you always kept some on hand
despite hating it yourself.

223
00:11:39,014 --> 00:11:41,171
I like how easy it is for
you to praise someone,

224
00:11:41,254 --> 00:11:42,871
even if you don't think you deserve any.

225
00:11:42,954 --> 00:11:46,751
And when you see someone meet with
misfortune, you always feel bad for them.

226
00:11:46,834 --> 00:11:48,611
I like that you cry for your friends,

227
00:11:48,694 --> 00:11:51,871
but still go out of your way to understand
and respect people's boundaries.

228
00:11:51,954 --> 00:11:55,511
You are by far the most loyal and
empathetic person I have ever met.

229
00:11:55,594 --> 00:11:58,151
You're oblivious to when others
hate you, so you don't reciprocate,

230
00:11:58,234 --> 00:12:00,171
though that obliviousness
can get you in trouble.

231
00:12:00,254 --> 00:12:01,831
I like that whenever you go out to eat,

232
00:12:01,914 --> 00:12:03,591
you go out of your way to
tell the staff that they

233
00:12:03,674 --> 00:12:06,291
did a good job and how
much you enjoyed the food.

234
00:12:06,374 --> 00:12:09,791
I like how much fun you can have when you're
at cultural festivals or doing sports,

235
00:12:09,874 --> 00:12:12,751
and how unexpectedly upset
you can get when you lose.

236
00:12:12,834 --> 00:12:16,031
I like that you think the unluckiest
fortune is actually lucky.

237
00:12:16,114 --> 00:12:18,191
Animals don't just like
you, they're drawn to you.

238
00:12:18,274 --> 00:12:20,551
I like that you always share
videos you think are funny,

239
00:12:20,634 --> 00:12:23,991
and how you can't stand horror movies
but force yourself through them anyway.

240
00:12:24,074 --> 00:12:26,251
I like that somehow you never
have a handkerchief on you,

241
00:12:26,334 --> 00:12:27,711
but you always make sure to have bandages.

242
00:12:27,794 --> 00:12:31,431
Your terrible taste in women and that
you're weirdly childlike I like that!

243
00:12:31,514 --> 00:12:33,131
You'll say it's a good day
just because the morning

244
00:12:33,214 --> 00:12:36,071
weather is nice and the way
you like Hokkaido and Okinawa?

245
00:12:36,154 --> 00:12:38,491
I like that despite how much
you complain about them.

246
00:12:38,574 --> 00:12:40,851
You care for your family more
than anything I like how much

247
00:12:40,934 --> 00:12:44,211
